    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **James Wood** (76.28) and **Brice Turang** (75.06) anchoring our lineup as the clear top-tier options. **James Wood** benefits from an elite xwOBA of 0.401 and a favorable matchup against Kelly, providing a massive 18% boost due to SP skill, while **Brice Turang** earns his status through a high-probability stolen base environment against Feltner; the combination of a slow pitcher delivery and a favorable batting order confirms him as our premier speed asset today. We are also leaning heavily into the platoon advantages of **Seiya Suzuki** (68.60) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (62.27), both of whom see significant bumps from the dynamic platoon projections against their respective right-handed starters.\n\nWhile **Josh Naylor** (61.01) and **Corbin Carroll** (60.87) provide solid production, the bench decision regarding **Zach McKinstry** (38.67) highlights our strict adherence to the efficiency floor. Despite **Zach McKinstry** having a respectable base projection, the combination of facing a tough arm in Woo and a bottom-order assignment dropped him well below our 40.0 benchmark, forcing a benching to preserve our limited game caps. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Austin Riley** (58.01) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (59.39), as both sit near the marginal threshold; **Austin Riley** specifically faces a risk profile dampened by an elite catcher\u2019s pop time, which threatens his stolen base upside and overall efficiency. Outside of our active roster, we remain monitoring **Trevor Story** and **Mickey Moniak**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us to rely on our active core to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings.",
